    "explanation": "The SGD 4.50 cancellation fee is refunded to the rider in full, and no driver compensation is payable. This is what both sides' filings in fact ask for, and the record supports it.\n\nWhy the fee cannot stand. The driver's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-02720, weight 1.0, admissibility COMPLETE, 100% coverage, 73 fixes at a 10 s cadence, no gaps) contains no fix inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius: the closest approach to the pickup pin is 53.08 m (driver_track.min_distance_m) and the derived arrival block reports qualifying_fix_count = 0 with a longest qualifying run of 0.0 s. POL-NS-01 limb (b) therefore fails. Because the driver's stationary position lay outside the arrival radius but within 400 m of the pin, POL-NS-03 governs and the fee is refunded in full; independently, POL-NS-06 refunds in full because the effective in-geofence dwell (0.0 s) falls 180 s short of the free waiting period in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180 s). Both figures are read from the brief.\n\nWhy the driver is not compensated. POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not. Under POL-NS-03 neither fault-allocation limb applies: the rider named no entrance, block or bay in the chat, so limb (i) does not arise, and trip_record.registered_pickup_points is 1, not 2 or more, so the pin-ambiguity goodwill of limb (ii) does not arise. No money is owed to the driver.\n\nThe driver's counterparty statement 'I was right at the pin' carries no weight_multiplier, enters neither the minimum nor the maximum of the confidence cap, and is contradicted by the trace. His 'I'm Here' tap at 12:31:25 and the platform's 180 s wait timer started at 12:31:27 record only that those markers were set; the trace shows his best approach was 53.08 m, so he did not reach the pin.\n\nClaims rejected on their merits. (1) Both sides invoke POL-NS-04 to exonerate the rider. It does not apply: limb (a) requires the rider's message to be locating or coordinating (her position, an entrance/block/bay, a request for the driver's position, or that she cannot see the vehicle), and the rider's only message, 'ok' at 12:32:55, is none of those, so the test fails at its first limb. The refund does not depend on this clause. (2) The POL-NS-05 false-arrival claim fails: the arrival marker is not shown false, since the driver's closest approach (53 m) is far inside the 300 m threshold and no 15 km/h-or-above reading is recorded at the arrival time. POL-NS-05 itself assigns a driver stationary within 300 m of the pin but outside the arrival radius to POL-NS-03, so no false-arrival referral arises. (3) Both sides correctly note that the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02720-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT), which makes POL-NS-06(i) accumulation unavailable; the absence is citable and cannot excuse the 180 s shortfall. (4) The driver-side profile check does not trip: no_show_terminations_30d = 1 against completed_trips_30d = 134, so POL-NS-07's anti-farming withholding does not engage, but it is irrelevant because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full.\n\nEvidence and confidence. The GPS trace, trip record and fare breakdown each carry weight 1.0, so the cap on the deciding facts is 1.0 and confidence is not driven below the floor; confidence is 0.95. No escalation trigger under POL-NS-09 fires: no admissible artifacts leave arrival unresolved (POL-NS-03 resolves them), both disputes_with_counterparty_90d counts are 0, rider no_show_disputes_30d is 0, the anti-farming check does not trip, and the only impaired artifact (the absent advisory) carries no deciding fact. The monetary effect of SGD 4.50 is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold and executes automatically under POL-GEN-05."
